[
	{
		"id": "c3b0000000003001",
		"type": "tab",
		"label": "vynst: turnstile, let the group in",
		"disabled": false,
		"info": "Turnstile with \"Gruppe einlassen\" (let the group in) behind a potential-free contact, e.g. the \"open\" input of a turnstile controller wired to a relay.\n\n1. Open \"vynst (inwendo ERP)\" and enter the address of your installation and an API token (right: events, write).\n2. Open the lock bridge once and press Done: instance id and secret are created. Deploy.\n3. In vynst: Settings > Smart locks, the Node-RED connection, \"Sync devices\". At the smart lock \"Drehkreuz\" switch on \"Leitung darf eine Gruppe einlassen\" and choose \"Bleibt offen\" or \"Einzelne Impulse\".\n4. Replace the debug node \"relay: turnstile contact\" by your relay (true = contact closed). Shelly: an mqtt out to shellies/<id>/relay/0/command with on / off.\n\nThe lock node keeps the time itself: stays open = \"hold_open\" (contact closed) until \"lock\" (contact open); single impulses = an \"open\" (contact closed for 0.5 s) every few seconds. A lost connection to vynst never leaves the turnstile open."
	},
